{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22: Derived candidate clean classification for positive winner values and 0<P<sum v: equality iff P<=min(v), or P>=sum of two largest v, or vA=vB=vC. Use D=sum v-P, w_i=min(v_i,D), y_i=w_i-(v_i-p_i). F becomes y>=0, sum y=H=sum w-D, y_i<=w_i; nearest is uniform y when feasible. Capped-simplex centroid has strict cap ordering whenever unequal smallest cap is active. Degenerate zero-value cases need separate treatment. Please review; no answer edit yet.' >> /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
