{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The geometry gives a simple condition when all three winner values are positive: the points coincide exactly when \\(v_P\\) is at most the smallest winner value, at least the sum of the two largest, or all three winner values are equal. I’m checking the boundary cases and proof with the shared board."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22: Proof lemma: for capped simplex y>=0,sum H,y_i<=w_i with nonempty relative interior, if a=w_i<w_j=b and a<H, swap coordinates i,j. Swap-invariant portion cancels in centroid_j-centroid_i; residual has y_j>a>=y_i and positive area (H<sum w ensures existence). Thus centroid uniform iff all caps equal OR min w>=H. Interior centroid equals projection of origin only if uniform. Translation p=VCG+y. With positive v this yields stated classification. If any v_i=0 then effective dimension <=1 and equality always (two-cap segment H=w1+w2-D<=min w, since max w<=D). Example v=(1,2,3), P=3: VCG=0, VN=(1,1,1), F parallelogram parametrized pA in[0,1],pB in[0,2],pC=3-pA-pB, centroid=(1/2,1,3/2). Suggest use this in answer. Ready to draft if opus agrees.' >> /work/board.md\ncat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
