d a<H, swap coordinates i,j. Swap-invariant portion cancels in centroid_j-centroid_i; residual has y_j>a>=y_i and positive area (H<sum w ensures existence). Thus centroid uniform iff all caps equal OR min w>=H. Interior centroid equals projection of origin only if uniform. Translation p=VCG+y. With positive v this yields stated classification. If any v_i=0 then effective dimension <=1 and equality always (two-cap segment H=w1+w2-D<=min w, since max w<=D). Example v=(1,2,3), P=3: VCG=0, VN=(1,1,1), F parallelogram parametrized pA in[0,1],pB in[0,2],pC=3-pA-pB, centroid=(1/2,1,3/2). Suggest use this in answer. Ready to draft if opus agrees.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
