{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 20:40: Complete proof draft at /work/sol-draft.md. Please review and either approve copying to answer.md or suggest changes. Includes strict swap proof, zero-value cases, and worked (1,2,3; P=3) parallelogram counterexample. We have ample time for independent numeric/proof audit.' >> /work/board.md\ncat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"[sol] 2026-10-22: Read problem. Deriving capped-simplex geometry and exact centroid/projection equality conditions independently; will post results and coordinate answer before editing.\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Derived candidate clean classification for positive winner values and 0<P<sum v: equality iff P<=min(v), or P>=sum of two largest v, or vA=vB=vC. Use D=sum v-P, w_i=min(v_i,D), y_i=w_i-(v_i-p_i). F becomes y>=0, sum y=H=sum w-D, y_i<=w_i; nearest is uniform y when feasible. Capped-simplex centroid has strict cap ordering whenever unequal smallest cap is active. Degenerate zero-value cases need separate treatment. Please review; no answer edit yet.\n[opus] 20:37 Reduction: with q_i=v_i-p_i, D=vA+vB+vC-vP, core = {0<=q_i<=v_i, sum q<=D}; F={sum q=D, 0<=q_i<=c_i}, c_i=min(v_i,D); VCG q=c. Vickrey-nearest = q_i=max(0,c_i-lam). Conjecture: equal iff caps symmetric (all v_i>=D, or all c_i equal...). Running numeric scan.\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Proof lemma: for capped simplex y>=0,sum H,y_i<=w_i with nonempty relative interior, if a=w_i<w_j=b and a<H, swap coordinates i,j. Swap-invariant portion cancels in centroid_j-centroid_i; residual has y_j>a>=y_i and positive area (H<sum w ensures existence). Thus centroid uniform iff all caps equal OR min w>=H. Interior centroid equals projection of origin only if uniform. Translation p=VCG+y. With positive v this yields stated classification. If any v_i=0 then effective dimension <=1 and equality always (two-cap segment H=w1+w2-D<=min w, since max w<=D). Example v=(1,2,3), P=3: VCG=0, VN=(1,1,1), F parallelogram parametrized pA in[0,1],pB in[0,2],pC=3-pA-pB, centroid=(1/2,1,3/2). Suggest use this in answer. Ready to draft if opus agrees.\n[sol] 20:38: I can write answer.md after your review/confirmation of classification. Exact full statement sorted 0<=a<=b<=c and P<sum: equality iff a=0 OR P<=a OR P>=b+c OR a=b=c. For positive values the centroid is interior, hence any nearest-centroid equality requires uniform y by stationarity. Will prepare a draft in /work/sol-draft.md meanwhile.\n[sol] 20:40: Complete proof draft at /work/sol-draft.md. Please review and either approve copying to answer.md or suggest changes. Includes strict swap proof, zero-value cases, and worked (1,2,3; P=3) parallelogram counterexample. We have ample time for independent numeric/proof audit.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /work/check_sol.py <<'PY'\nfrom fractions import Fraction as Q\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef clip(poly, f):\n    out=[]\n    if not poly: return out\n    for a,b in zip(poly,poly[1:]+poly[:1]):\n        fa,fb=f(a),f(b)\n        if fa>=0: out.append(a)\n        if (fa<0<fb) or (fb<0<fa):\n            t=fa/(fa-fb)\n            out.append(tuple(x+t*(y-x) for x,y in zip(a,b)))\n    return out\n\ndef centroid(v,P):\n    a,b,c=v\n    poly=[(Q(0),Q(0)),(a,Q(0)),(a,b),(Q(0),b)]\n    poly=clip(poly,lambda p:P-p[0]-p[1])\n    poly=clip(poly,lambda p:c-P+p[0]+p[1])\n    z=sum(x*Y-X*y for (x,y),(X,Y) in zip(poly,poly[1:]+poly[:1]))\n    m=[]\n    for k in range(2):\n        m.append(sum((p[k]+q[k])*(p[0]*q[1]-q[0]*p[1]) for p,q in zip(poly,poly[1:]+poly[:1]))/(3*z))\n    return (*m,P-sum(m))\n\ndef vn(v,P):\n    D=sum(v)-P\n    w=[min(x,D) for x in v]\n    lo=[x-y for x,y in zip(v,w)]\n    H=P-sum(lo)\n    order=sorted(range(3),key=lambda i:w[i]); rem=H; y=[Q(0)]*3\n    for n,i in enumerate(order):\n        t=rem/(3-n)\n        if t<=w[i]:\n            for j in order[n:]: y[j]=t\n            break\n        y[i]=w[i]; rem-=w[i]\n    return tuple(x+z for x,z in zip(lo,y))\n\ncount=0\nfor vs in product(range(1,9),repeat=3):\n    v=tuple(map(Q,vs)); a,b,c=sorted(v)\n    for k in range(1,int(2*sum(v))):\n        P=Q(k,2)\n        expected=P<=a or P>=b+c or a==b==c\n        equal=centroid(v,P)==vn(v,P)\n        assert expected==equal,(v,P,centroid(v,P),vn(v,P),expected)\n        count+=1\nprint(f'Exact rational polygon/projection checks passed: {count} cases.')\nPY\npython /work/check_sol.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /work/check_sol.py <<'PY'\nfrom fractions import Fraction as Q\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef clip(poly, f):\n    out=[]\n    if not poly: return out\n    for a,b in zip(poly,poly[1:]+poly[:1]):\n        fa,fb=f(a),f(b)\n        if fa>=0: out.append(a)\n        if (fa<0<fb) or (fb<0<fa):\n            t=fa/(fa-fb)\n            out.append(tuple(x+t*(y-x) for x,y in zip(a,b)))\n    return out\n\ndef centroid(v,P):\n    a,b,c=v\n    poly=[(Q(0),Q(0)),(a,Q(0)),(a,b),(Q(0),b)]\n    poly=clip(poly,lambda p:P-p[0]-p[1])\n    poly=clip(poly,lambda p:c-P+p[0]+p[1])\n    z=sum(x*Y-X*y for (x,y),(X,Y) in zip(poly,poly[1:]+poly[:1]))\n    m=[]\n    for k in range(2):\n        m.append(sum((p[k]+q[k])*(p[0]*q[1]-q[0]*p[1]) for p,q in zip(poly,poly[1:]+poly[:1]))/(3*z))\n    return (*m,P-sum(m))\n\ndef vn(v,P):\n    D=sum(v)-P\n    w=[min(x,D) for x in v]\n    lo=[x-y for x,y in zip(v,w)]\n    H=P-sum(lo)\n    order=sorted(range(3),key=lambda i:w[i]); rem=H; y=[Q(0)]*3\n    for n,i in enumerate(order):\n        t=rem/(3-n)\n        if t<=w[i]:\n            for j in order[n:]: y[j]=t\n            break\n        y[i]=w[i]; rem-=w[i]\n    return tuple(x+z for x,z in zip(lo,y))\n\ncount=0\nfor vs in product(range(1,9),repeat=3):\n    v=tuple(map(Q,vs)); a,b,c=sorted(v)\n    for k in range(1,int(2*sum(v))):\n        P=Q(k,2)\n        expected=P<=a or P>=b+c or a==b==c\n        equal=centroid(v,P)==vn(v,P)\n        assert expected==equal,(v,P,centroid(v,P),vn(v,P),expected)\n        count+=1\nprint(f'Exact rational polygon/projection checks passed: {count} cases.')\nPY\npython /work/check_sol.py\"","aggregated_output":"Exact rational polygon/projection checks passed: 13312 cases.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
