D). Example v=(1,2,3), P=3: VCG=0, VN=(1,1,1), F parallelogram parametrized pA in[0,1],pB in[0,2],pC=3-pA-pB, centroid=(1/2,1,3/2). Suggest use this in answer. Ready to draft if opus agrees.\n[sol] 20:38: I can write answer.md after your review/confirmation of classification. Exact full statement sorted 0<=a<=b<=c and P<sum: equality iff a=0 OR P<=a OR P>=b+c OR a=b=c. For positive values the centroid is interior, hence any nearest-centroid equality requires uniform y by stationarity. Will prepare a draft in /work/sol-draft.md meanwhile.\n[sol] 20:40: Complete proof draft at /work/sol-draft.md. Please review and either approve copying to answer.md or suggest changes. Includes strict swap proof, zero-value cases, and worked (1,2,3; P=3) parallelogram counterexample. We have ample time for independent numeric/proof audit.\n[opus] 20:38 AGREE with sol's classification. Numeric scan of 200k random instances (polygon centroid vs projection) matches it; only mismatches are float noise at P~1e-4. Also verified sol's example (1,2,3),P=3. Extra example with mixed caps: v=(4,3,2), P=5: D=4, VCG=(0,0,0), VN p=(5/3,5/3,5/3), centroid p=(7/3, 53/33, 35/33). Note interior-vs-boundary: when uniform y infeasible, VN lies on boundary of F while centroid is in relative interior, so they differ too. sol: please draft answer.md; I'll review.\n[sol] 20:41: Independent exact-arithmetic audit passed 13,312 cases: all ordered positive integer triples in 1..8, all admissible positive half-integer P. Polygon centroid computed by rational clipping/shoelace; VN by capped water filling. Script /work/check_sol.py. Classification and examples match exactly.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
